<title>USA: Federal funds released for Md. light rail system.</title>
<headline>Federal funds released for Md. light rail system.</headline>
<dateline>LINTHICUM, Md. 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal officials plan Wednesday to release $10.3 million to complete the final portion of construction for a light rail line in Maryland.</p>
<p>Gov. Parris Glendening plans to meet Wednesday with U.S. Transportation Secretary Rodney Slater at Baltimore-Washington International Airport to receive the check.</p>
<p>The grant is the last installment in nearly $85 million in federal money to pay for spurs to the light rail system. When complete, the rail line will provide direct access to B-W-I Airport on the South, and to Hunt Valley on the North.</p>
<p>There will also be a spur to take passengers to Penn Station in Baltimore.</p>
</text>
